mundane theorem abs-bounds
  note        |x| is x or −x, whichever is not negative, so it is at least
              both.
  let x ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  then x ≤ |x|. −x ≤ |x|.

1.  x ≥ 0 or x < 0
    mun:nonneg-or-neg

2.  x ≤ |x|. −x ≤ |x|.
    cases, from 1

    case
    assume x ≥ 0                                                      (C1)

    2.1.  |x| = x
          mun:abs, from C1

    2.2.  x ≤ |x|
          inequalities
            |x| = x          2.1
            x = |x|          symmetry
            x ≤ |x|          weakening

    2.3.  −x ≤ 0
          inequalities
            x ≥ 0            C1
            −x ≤ 0           multiplying by −1

    2.4.  −x ≤ |x|
          transitivity, from 2.3, C1, 2.1

    2.5.  x ≤ |x|. −x ≤ |x|.
          join 2.2, 2.4

    case
    assume x < 0                                                      (C2)

    2.6.  |x| = −x
          mun:abs, from C2

    2.7.  −x ≤ |x|
          inequalities
            |x| = −x         2.6
            −x = |x|         symmetry
            −x ≤ |x|         weakening

    2.8.  0 < −x
          inequalities
            x < 0            C2
            −x > 0           multiplying by −1
            0 < −x           symmetry

    2.9.  x < |x|
          transitivity, from C2, 2.8, 2.6

    2.10. x ≤ |x|
          inequalities
            x < |x|          2.9
            x ≤ |x|          weakening
          requires |x| ∈ ℝ: mun:abs-real

    2.11. x ≤ |x|. −x ≤ |x|.
          join 2.7, 2.10
